  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1247 PM CDT Fri Oct 23 2026\n\nPersistence forecast continues as an upper level ridge continues\nto expand into the northern Plains. The ridge will gradually be\nsquashed due to a deepening upper trough across the Pacific\nNorthwest. This will keep temperatures in the upper 70s and lower\n80s through Saturday, but will result in weak return flow. A\nslight increase in moisture will raise relative humidity values\nat or above 30% on Saturday finally providing some relief from\nthe elevated fire danger.\n\nAs the ridge continues to be influenced by the aforementioned\ntrough, this will extend a cirrus shield and should moderate\ntemperatures slightly and cap high temperatures at or below\n80 degrees. We will remain in easterly/northerly flow aloft which\nalso supports a slight cool down. Confidence remains high in dry\nconditions and above normal temperatures persisting through the\nweekend and into early next week.\n\nConfidence lowers into the middle of next week as model guidance\ncontinues to disagree on the evolution of the trough and various\nshortwaves in association. While details do remain uncertain, the\nClimate Prediction Center has highlighted the Mid-South to end\nOctober and kick off November with above normal temperatures (70-\n80% chance) and above normal precipitation (40-50% chance).\n\nDNM",
